                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Californium is a stylish walking simulator that prioritizes its cool visuals and dialogue. Gameplay consists of taking to people and looking for hidden instances of the Greek letter Theta - Θ. Seeing how a small cast of characters change through a series of different universes is the main point of enjoyment for me. \n\nThere's also a small segment at the start of each chapter where the player needs to type text that is written by the protagonist that informs the player about the world the player is exploring. My main complaint about that segment is that it only requires pushing the letter keys while spaces between words and punctuation are automatically imputed. It threw me off each time.\n\nIt's a fairly short game and during that time I did walk through a wall texture once and fall through the ground once. I respawned in the normal play area with no loss of progress so it's not too bad of an oversight all things considered.",
